DECISIONS 339, CODEGEN.md §2.1, §5.2: an `ordered` enum cannot be opened (`openOrdered`): its Go string type would compare members by text, not in declaration order.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// A tier.
enum Tier ordered { low, high }

emit go { out: "@sovcommon/a", mode: types, open: [Tier] }
-- findings.txt --
error[E8009]  a/a.canon:6:52
  open of emit go: Tier is ordered, and an open enum cannot compare its members

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
